# mcp-tools-list-hidden-command - a plugin command marked Hidden must not appear
# in the MCP tools/list result.
#
# VALIDATES: a CommandDecl with hidden true reaches no MCP client, while a
# non-hidden command from the same plugin does reach every MCP client.
#
# ai/rules/cli-patterns.md documents Hidden as "suppress a command". The
# completion tree obeyed that through CommandRegistry.VisibleCommandEntries, and
# the MCP surface did not. buildCommandMeta (cmd/ze/hub/command_meta.go) merges
# the dispatcher commands with the plugin command registry. It read no Hidden
# field, so every hidden plugin command became an MCP tool action.
#
# PREVENTS: an MCP client that sees a plugin command which operators cannot see
# in completion or help. The same merged list feeds the API command list, so one
# producer leaked the command to two surfaces.
#
# The two assertions have separate jobs. The reject is the defect assertion. The
# token "concealed" names the hidden command, its description, and its action
# enum value, so one reject covers every place the leak can surface. The expect
# is the vacuity guard. It holds in both states, and it goes red when the plugin
# registers nothing. Without it a daemon that starts no plugin passes the reject
# and proves nothing.

# Native fixture registers one visible and one hidden command and remains
# attached until daemon shutdown.

# wait-tool polls tools/list until the tool exists, so the test waits for the
# plugin registration instead of a fixed duration. The tool name comes from the
# "show mcpgate" prefix through toolName (internal/component/mcp/tools.go).
stdin=mcp:terminator=EOF_MCP
wait-tool ze_show_mcpgate
probe tools/list
EOF_MCP

stdin=ze-conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external mcpgate-test {
		run "ze-test fixture plugin/mcp-tools-list-hidden-command"
		encoder json
	}
}

bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept false
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 1
				remote 1
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze --mcp $PORT -:stdin=ze-conf
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze-test mcp --port $PORT:stdin=mcp:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=probe status=200 code=ok
expect=stdout:contains=ze_show_mcpgate
expect=stdout:contains=visible probe command
reject=stdout:contains=concealed
